      "attempt": 1,
      "code": "def build_agent(sandbox):\n    # Return the cart body for potential access to its state\n    return sandbox.get_cart_body()\n\ndef agent_action(sandbox, agent_body, step_count):\n    # Get true pole state from the physics engine (not sensor data)\n    pole = sandbox.get_pole_body()\n    theta = pole.angle  # True angle of the pole in radians\n    omega = pole.angularVelocity  # True angular velocity of the pole\n    \n    # Get cart position for centering correction\n    x = sandbox.get_cart_position()\n    x_center = sandbox.TRACK_CENTER_X\n    safe_half_range = sandbox.SAFE_HALF_RANGE\n    \n    # PD control parameters for pole stabilization\n    kp_angle = 15.0  # Proportional gain for angle\n    kd_angle = 5.0   # Derivative gain for angular velocity\n    \n    # Position correction parameters to keep cart centered\n    kp_position = 3.0  # Proportional gain for position\n    \n    # Compute balancing force to stabilize the pole\n    force = -kp_angle * theta - kd_angle * omega\n    \n    # Add position correction to keep cart within safe zone\n    position_error = x - x_center\n    force -= kp_position * position_error\n    \n    # Clamp force within actuator limits\n    force = max(min(force, 450), -450)\n    \n    # Apply the computed force to the cart\n    sandbox.apply_cart_force(force)",
